From 6841e6f75603885c380ed66268ada85d15a9957a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneplus-nord2t-karen contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:44:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: validate the DVFSRC device data

The interrupt-log store handler fetched its device data without using it,
which Clang rejects in this warning-as-error build. Match the neighboring
sysfs handler by rejecting access when the device data is unavailable.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 drivers/devfreq/helio-dvfsrc-v3/helio-dvfsrc-sysfs.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/helio-dvfsrc-v3/helio-dvfsrc-sysfs.c b/drivers/devfreq/helio-dvfsrc-v3/helio-dvfsrc-sysfs.c
index e7f28aa..c07a5f1 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/helio-dvfsrc-v3/helio-dvfsrc-sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/helio-dvfsrc-v3/helio-dvfsrc-sysfs.c
@@ -256 +256,4 @@
-	dvfsrc = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	dvfsrc = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	if (!dvfsrc)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
